	(lib_symbols

	)
	(text_box "WHAT THIS PROJECT IS, AND WHAT THESE FIVE SHEETS SETTLE\n\nTwo nodes and one radio link. A BASE STATION bolted permanently to a roof, and a ROVER: a hand-pushed\ncart that logs a GNSS epoch five times a second while somebody walks it over 0.69 acres of lawn, pine\nstraw and gravel. Post-processed against the base, the rover produces full-property elevation and a\ngenuinely located tree line - the half of the job a 2D boundary survey does not answer.\n\nTHIS IS AN INTEGRATION DESIGN, NOT AN RF DESIGN. The receiver is bought, the antenna is bought, the\nradio is bought. Nothing here designs a receiver front end or a filter. What these sheets settle is\neverything around those parts: which UART carries what, what powers what, where the antenna reference\npoint physically is, how far the transmitter has to sit from the GNSS antenna, and what happens to a\nhalf-written log record when the battery stops.\n\n                                     ~ 75 m\n    +---------------------------+   RTCM3    +----------------------------+\n    |  BASE  (roof, permanent)  | =========> |  ROVER  (cart, hand-pushed)|\n    |                           |  915 MHz   |                            |\n    |  ANN-MB-00 on the ridge   |  FHSS      |  ANN-MB-00 on a 0.5 m mast |\n    |    | 5 m RG-174           |  broadcast |    | 5 m RG-174            |\n    |  ZED-F9P  UART2 -> RTCM3 out           |  ZED-F9P  UART2 <- RTCM3 in|\n    |           UART1 -> raw obs             |           UART1 -> PVT+raw |\n    |  Arduino Due  -> XBee TX               |  XBee RX  -> Arduino Due   |\n    |  microSD: raw observations, always     |  microSD: epoch records    |\n    |  Mains + pass-through bank as a UPS    |  5 V USB power bank        |\n    +---------------------------+            +----------------------------+\n                    \\                                    /\n                     \\____  both logs meet at the desk  _/\n                              PPK reprocessing\n\nWHY THE LINK IS ONE-WAY. The rover never has to answer. Corrections are broadcast base -> rover with\nno acknowledgement, which means the ROVER'S RADIO NEVER TRANSMITS, which in turn means it can never\ndesense the GNSS antenna sitting half a metre from it. The cost is that the base cannot know the rover\nmissed a message - and that cost is already paid, because PPK reprocesses the whole session from raw\nobservations at the desk. A dropped correction degrades the live display and nothing else. See the\nantenna sheet for the arithmetic that makes this worth doing."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 15.24 0)
		(size 122.1768 75.009)
		(margins 1.27 1.27 1.27 1.27)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
