	(text_box "ONE NODE DESIGN, BUILT TWICE - AND THAT IS THE POINT\n\nThe base and the rover are the SAME schematic. Same MCU, same receiver board, same radio, same storage,\nsame pin assignment. UART2 is wired in both directions at both ends; which direction carries traffic is\na firmware choice, not a wiring difference. One bring-up serves both nodes, and the pin table below is\nthe only pin table this project has.\n\n  what differs           base                              rover\n  --------------------   -------------------------------   ---------------------------------\n  power source           mains + pass-through bank (UPS)    5 V USB power bank\n  field indicator        RGB LED only                       RGB LED + memory LCD + buzzer\n                                                            + mark button\n  antenna mount          roof ridge, forced centering       0.5 m mast on the cart\n  radio                  transmits (PL=0, +7 dBm)           receive-only, never keys up\n  fault policy (#50/#52) reset - unattended, keep serving    stop and say so - a human is there\n\nEverything else is identical, including the parts that look like they should not be. The rover carries\na radio it never transmits with, because the module is the same part number and populating it costs\nnothing; the base carries an RGB LED nobody watches, because a person on a ladder wants to know the box\nis alive before they climb back down."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 95.329 0)
		(size 123.3452 44.148)
		(margins 1.27 1.27 1.27 1.27)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 222 245 222 1)
		)
		(effects
