	(text_box "THE MODULE PURCHASING DECISION - AND IMU TILT COMPENSATION, DECIDED: OUT OF SCOPE\n\nBOUGHT: u-blox ZED-F9P, on a SparkFun GPS-RTK-SMA carrier (GPS-16481), at both nodes. It is a plain\nmulti-band RTK positioning module. It has no IMU, no dead reckoning and no tilt compensation, and that\nis a decision made here rather than a discovery left for the rover story.\n\nTHE PROBLEM TILT COMPENSATION WOULD SOLVE. The antenna sits 0.5 m above the ground point it is\nreporting. Tilt the mast by 10 degrees and the antenna moves 0.5 x sin(10 deg) = 8.7 cm horizontally\nwhile the wheels have not moved at all. A survey pole is bubble-levelled by a human at every shot; a\ncart crossing roots and leaf litter is levelled by nobody. 8.7 cm is the same order as the entire rest\nof the error budget, so this is not a rounding term.\n\nWHAT WAS ACTUALLY CHECKED, RATHER THAN ASSUMED.\n\n  u-blox ZED-F9P    NO. \"The ZED-F9P firmware does not support the dead reckoning position fix type\"\n                    (Integration manual UBX-18010802 R16, section 3.1.8.3). There is no IMU on the\n                    module and no firmware option that adds one.\n  u-blox ZED-F9R    NOT THIS. It fuses an internal 6-axis IMU with GNSS AND WHEEL TICKS, and its\n                    integration manual (UBX-20039643 R10, section 3.1.10.1) says the algorithm is\n                    \"optimized for automotive, e-scooter, rail vehicle and robotic lawn mower\n                    platforms only\". It also demands an initial calibration drive. This is vehicle\n                    dead reckoning, not pole-tip compensation; the words \"tilt\", \"survey\" and \"pole\"\n                    do not appear in either F9R document.\n  Unicore UM980     NO. Neither its datasheet nor its user manual mentions tilt, IMU or inertial\n                    anything. The board people associate with tilt - SparkFun's RTK Torch - gets it\n                    from a SEPARATE IM19 inertial module, not from the receiver.\n  UM981S / Torch    YES, and at USD 2,149.95 for the Torch against USD 259.95 for a ZED-F9P carrier.\n                    Two nodes: about USD 4,300 against about USD 520.\n\nAND THE FINDING THAT SETTLES IT, WHICH IS NOT THE PRICE. Every documented tilt-compensation\ninitialisation procedure assumes A SURVEY POLE WITH ITS TIP PLANTED ON THE GROUND. The IM19\nintegration guide's working modes are \"shaking the RTK pole back and forth with the end of pole fixed\non the ground\"; SparkFun's Torch firmware hard-codes that mode, and its user procedure is: get an RTK\nFIX, enter the pole length, shake vertically, plant the tip, rock the head up to 30 degrees. Then:\n\"Tilt Compensation mode will be exited if RTK Fix is lost.\"\n\n  A CART CANNOT PERFORM THAT RITUAL. It has no tip to plant and nobody to shake it. And the exit\n  condition is fatal to the whole idea here: tilt compensation switches itself off exactly when the\n  fix drops - which is under the canopy, which is where the tilt error and the terrain both matter\n  most. It would be present in the open lawn where it is not needed and absent under the pines where\n  it is.\n\nSO THE REJECTION IS NOT \"TOO EXPENSIVE\", IT IS \"DOES NOT APPLY\". A cart with a rigidly mounted,\nnear-vertical antenna does not have the problem tilt compensation was built for; it has a small,\nslow, terrain-driven tilt, and the levers for that are mechanical: shorten the mast (4.3 cm at 0.25 m\ninstead of 8.7 cm at 0.5 m), stiffen it, or hang it in a damped gimbal. All three are cheaper than a\ndifferent receiver and none of them stops working when the fix drops.\n\nWHAT THIS COMMITS US TO. The rover applies a FIXED ARP -> ground offset (antenna sheet) and records it\nper epoch. Residual tilt is not corrected and not modelled; #54 measures it by driving over monumented\niron pipes held to 2.4 cm, and the write-up publishes it as part of the accuracy claim. That is an\nhonest 10 cm instrument rather than a silent one - and if tilt turns out to dominate, the first lever\nis the mast, not the module."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 144.557 0)
