	(text_box "ELECTRICAL CEILINGS - the rows #50 and #52 copy into resource-budget.md section 4\n\nEvery figure below is a datasheet maximum, not a measurement. Section 4 of the repo template\n(docs/resource-budget.md) wants ceiling / budget / headroom; the ceiling and the budget are here, and\n#54 replaces the budget column with measured numbers.\n\n  quantity                                     ceiling        budget (worst case)   headroom   source\n  ------------------------------------------   ------------   -------------------   --------   --------------------------\n  I/O voltage on any Due pin                   3.3 V          3.3 V                 0 %        Due A000062 5.1 safety note\n  ZED-F9P input pin voltage                    VCC (3.3 V)    3.3 V                 0 %        F9P Table 15, Vin 0..VCC\n  XBee supply voltage                          3.6 V          3.3 V                 8 %        XBee UG A-01\n  microSD supply voltage                       2.7 .. 3.6 V   3.3 V                 -          SD Phys. Layer 9.10, sec. 2\n  memory LCD panel supply                      4.8 .. 5.5 V   5.0 V                 -          Sharp LCP-2110015A Table 7-1\n  Source current, Due Group 1 pin              -15 mA         -0.62 mA (LED base)   96 %       SAM3X Table 45-2 note 2\n  Source current, Due Group 2 pin              -3 mA          -0.05 mA (UART TX)    98 %       SAM3X Table 45-2 note 3\n  Sink current, Due Group 1 pin                9 mA           0.05 mA               99 %       SAM3X Table 45-2\n  Total DC output current, all Due I/O         130 mA         4.0 mA                97 %       SAM3X Table 45-1, 144-LQFP\n  DC current, any ZED-F9P digital I/O pin      5 mA           0.05 mA               99 %       F9P Table 15\n  Antenna bias current out of VCC_RF           50 mA          15 mA typ             70 %       F9P Table 15 / ANN-MB Table 2\n  Antenna bias voltage AT THE ANTENNA          3.0 .. 5.0 V   2.7 V as shipped      FAILS      see the antenna sheet\n  External gain seen at RF_IN                  17 .. 50 dB    21.4 dB typ           4.4 dB     F9P Table 15 / ANN-MB Table 2\n                                                                                    over floor\n  Input power at RF_IN                         +10 dBm        -44 dBm at 1 m        54 dB      F9P Table 14 / antenna sheet\n  microSD supply current, SPI mode             100 mA         100 mA                0 %        SD Phys. Layer 9.10 Table 3-6\n  Due 3V3 rail load                            see note       238 mA                -          power sheet\n  Due board normal-mode current                130 .. 800 mA  462 mA                42 %       Due A000062 section 5.3\n  Node draw at 5 V, average                    -              rover 330 mA          -          power sheet\n                                                              base  295 mA\n  Node draw at 5 V, worst case burst           -              462 mA                -          power sheet\n  Radio conducted output power                 +24 dBm max    +7 dBm (PL=0)         17 dB      XBee UG PL command\n  SPI clock, shared bus                        2 MHz          2 MHz with the LCD    0 %        Sharp Table 6-3-1\n                                                              8 MHz with the card              SD spec\n\nTHREE OF THESE HAVE NO MARGIN AT ALL AND ARE THE ONES WORTH READING TWICE.\n\n  3.3 V on a Due pin. 5 V damages the board, and +5 V sits at position 1 of both D22-D53 headers and\n  position 2 of the ICSP header.\n\n  +10 dBm at RF_IN is an ABSOLUTE MAXIMUM on the receiver's antenna input, not a derating. The antenna\n  sheet shows what has to be true for the radio not to exceed it, and what breaks if a cheaper antenna\n  is substituted.\n\n  THE ANTENNA BIAS VOLTAGE FAILS AS SHIPPED. The chosen carrier board feeds the antenna through a\n  33 ohm series resistor, which at the antenna's 15 mA drops 0.5 V and lands 0.3 V BELOW its minimum\n  supply. This is the one row in this table that is not satisfied by the parts as bought. The antenna\n  sheet carries the arithmetic, the bring-up measurement that confirms it, and the fix."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 431.8 15.24 0)
