	(text_box "THE UNDER-CANOPY BET, TAKEN DELIBERATELY - AND THE WAY OUT IF IT LOSES\n\nThere is no feasibility spike ahead of this story. Hardware is being committed before anyone knows\nwhether RTK holds a fix under these pines. That is a bet, and it is recorded here rather than\ndiscovered later.\n\nWHAT IS ALREADY SAFE. The boundary half of the original job is answered - a Class A VRS RTK boundary\nsurvey exists at 0.08 ft (2.4 cm) horizontal, about four times better than this rover will ever be.\nNothing here needs to re-measure a corner.\n\nWHAT IS EXPOSED. The topography half is untouched by that survey - the tell is the letter H in\n\"positional accuracy: H 0.08'\", a horizontal figure with no vertical companion, no datum, no benchmark\nand no contour anywhere on the sheet. Elevation is the whole reason this rover exists, and elevation is\nexactly what degrades under canopy.\n\nTHE SHAPE OF THE LOSS, IF IT LOSES. Roughly two thirds of the parcel is open. A total under-canopy\nfailure therefore does not produce a dead project; it produces a complete, uniform, current surface over\nthe open two thirds and HOLES under the pines. Holes are a known deficiency of a real dataset. That is a\ncategorically better failure than a plausible one, which is why #51 makes per-epoch solution status\nstructurally impossible to omit: a FLOAT excursion under canopy is smooth and correlated and looks\nexactly like a gentle hollow in the ground.\n\nTHE ESCAPE ROUTE, NAMED NOW SO IT IS NOT A SURPRISE LATER. UWB ranging anchors placed on the monumented\niron pipes. UWB does not care about sky view, the monuments are already surveyed to 2.4 cm, and the\nrover already carries an MCU with spare UARTs and a spare SPI chip select. It is a different instrument\nbolted to the same cart, not a redesign. It is not being built now, and it is not being designed here -\nit is recorded as the thing to reach for if #53's tree-line mission comes back saying the wooded third\nnever fixes."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 431.8 117.9604 0)
		(size 124.5136 60.6072)
		(margins 1.27 1.27 1.27 1.27)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 214 214 1)
		)
