				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5d1c0000-0006-4000-8000-000000000006")
	)
	(text_box "HOW TO READ THESE SHEETS\n\n  rtk-node       one node, drawn once, built twice. The MCU, the receiver board, the radio, the card,\n                 the pin assignment table and the two places a jumper can be miscounted.\n  rtk-antenna    the antenna, its coax and its bias; the antenna reference point and the ARP -> ground\n                 offset that the rover subtracts from every epoch; and the radio/GNSS coexistence\n                 arithmetic that sets the minimum antenna separation.\n  rtk-power      both power plans, the achievable session length, and the brownout and write-path\n                 hazard that the rover's fault policy depends on.\n  rtk-indicator  the rover's field indicator: what the operator can see with their hands on the handle.\n\nNETS CROSS SHEETS BY GLOBAL LABEL. +3V3, +5V and GND are global, as are the signals that leave the node\nsheet for the indicator, the antenna and the power sheets. There are no hierarchical sheet pins; the\nnetlist is the proof of connectivity, and\n\n    kicad-cli sch export netlist --format kicadsexpr rtk.kicad_sch\n\nis how you check that TX really did land on RX."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 431.8 183.6476 0)
		(size 123.3452 40.0332)
		(margins 1.27 1.27 1.27 1.27)
		(stroke
			(width 0.254)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 238 238 238 1)
		)
		(effects
